  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader, I want the topic list to look the same whatever the filter (\"Tous\", \"Favoris\", \"Suivis\", \"Lus\"), so that switching filters does not change the layout under me. (Operator feedback, 2026-11-13.)\n\n### Observed\n\nIn a topic list, the \"Tous\" filter and the \"Favoris / Suivis / Lus\" filters do not show the same UI: rows, layout and decorations differ between them.\n\n### Expected\n\n- One row and list presentation for every filter. Only the content changes; elements that only make sense in a filter (for example the flag icon) are allowed if they sit in the same layout.\n- The reference is legacy at `87fe0d1c` for the same lists (parity first). Cite it in the PR.\n\n### Scope\n\n- The same row component as group L (#817, #825, #647, #648) and #803 (visual consistency of the card lists, claimed on the Mac). Coordinate with #803 before starting.\n- This is exactly the duplication case of #836. Fix it in one shared component, never one copy per filter.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] All four filters use the same row and list component; Mac screenshots of each filter, light and dark, are posted on the PR.\n- [ ] A test pins that each filter renders through the shared component.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
